Examples: Approve a new user: echo '{"status": "approved"}' | fabric agent-gateway users update \ <user-id> --file -

Make a user a power user and set their job title: fabric agent-gateway users update <user-id> --file user.json where user.json is: {"role": "poweruser", "job_title": "Platform engineer"}

Disable a user, which also ends their sessions: echo '{"status": "disabled"}' | fabric agent-gateway users update \ <user-id> --file -

Examples: Check a remote key set, then create a strategy that uses it: JWKS=https://idp.example.com/.well-known/jwks.json fabric agent-gateway jwt-verification-strategies validate-jwks-uri "$JWKS" fabric agent-gateway jwt-verification-strategies create --file strategy.json where strategy.json is: { "name": "Partner IdP", "expected_issuer": "https://idp.example.com/", "jwks_source": { "type": "remote", "jwks_uri": "https://idp.example.com/.well-known/jwks.json" } }

Pin the keys in the document instead of fetching them: "jwks_source": { "type": "static", "jwks": [{"kty": "RSA", "kid": "2026-09", "n": "...", "e": "AQAB"}] }

Change a strategy: save it, edit it, send it back: fabric agent-gateway jwt-verification-strategies get <id> --output json > \ strategy.json fabric agent-gateway jwt-verification-strategies update <id> \ --file strategy.json
